.TH UU-REMOTE-FOR-LINUX 1 "@RELEASE_DATE@" "uu-remote-for-linux @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uu-remote-for-linux \- run NetEase UU Remote through an isolated Wine prefix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uu-remote-for-linux
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ client-arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uu-remote-for-linux
downloads the official NetEase UU Remote Windows client on first setup and
runs it in an isolated Wine prefix with native Linux tray, input, update,
multi-monitor, X11, and GNOME Wayland integration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --accept-eula
Accept the NetEase UU Remote license and continue with first-time setup.
.TP
.B --setup-only
Install or repair the Wine prefix without starting the client.
.TP
.B --check-update
Check for and install the latest official client version immediately.
.TP
.B --show
Show the main window of an already running client.
.TP
.B --stop
Stop the isolated UU Remote Wine prefix and managed user services.
.TP
.B --diagnose
Print read-only compatibility and runtime diagnostics.
.TP
.B --wayland-keyboard-status
Inspect eligibility for the bundled, version-matched Mutter repair.
.TP
.B --repair-wayland-keyboard
Show the opt-in system keyboard repair dialog again. The installed Debian
package includes patched packages, original rollback packages and full source.
Application requires administrator authentication and a later logout/login.
.TP
.B --rollback-wayland-keyboard
Prompt to restore the original Mutter packages and package holds saved by this
tool. Neither operation automatically restarts the graphical session.
.TP
.B --list-decoders
List detected decoding devices and capabilities.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete command-line option list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/uu-remote-for-linux
Wine prefix and persistent compatibility state.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/uu-remote-for-linux
Runtime status and diagnostic logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wine (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Wenqi Guo and contributors.
